en  these policies and guidelines were  issued and what the government knew at  the time they can't pretend they didn't  know the risk to care homes they  absolutely did know the risk at the  daily briefing NHS England defended  testing policies I'm absolutely sure  that my medical colleagues would not be  discharging patients under any  circumstances unless they were sure that  their medical treatments in hospital was  complete they were fit for discharge and  it was safe to discharge them in spite  of the admission of one Minister many  care homes say greater support is still  needed if they're to keep vulnerable  people in care home safe Lisa Holland  Sky News Birmingham
 

